  "necessity_paragraph": "The patient presents with recurrent episodes of palpitations and lightheadedness consistent with supraventricular tachycardia, occurring against a background of known atherosclerotic heart disease of the native coronary artery (I25.10). Mobile cardiac telemetry (CPT 93229) is ordered to capture intermittent arrhythmic events and correlate symptoms with rhythm disturbances in an outpatient setting. This service is medically necessary to evaluate the recurrent palpitations and lightheadedness in the context of the documented supraventricular tachycardia and underlying coronary artery disease. The denial under CO-197 for missing precertification is contested because the clinical indication clearly supports the need for Mobile Cardiac Telemetry monitoring (CPT 93229) to correlate the patient's symptoms with rhythm disturbances."
